messages:
ana (Docs): Opening PR to standardize SOC2-friendly wording for audit logs + add C# and PHP SDK export snippets. Link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5092
kevin (Security): Thanks. Two quick asks: 1) avoid 'tenant' in public copy; use 'customer' 2) call out that deletions may be delayed due to backup cycles and lawful holds.
nana (Docs): (typo) I meant 'ana' :) Draft sentence: "Redwood retains audit logs according to customer-defined retention policies; export and deletion requests are fulfilled, subject to lawful holds and contractual obligations."
leo (Legal): That reads fine. Prefer 'fulfilled' to 'processed' for consumer-facing docs. Add 'contractual obligations' as you have.
nana (Docs): Updated in PR. Also planning to switch TTL examples to ISO 8601 durations (P30D, P90D, P365D) instead of '30/90/365 days'.
maya (DevEx): I'll add C# and PHP code snippets. Question: should we show both streaming (async) and paged examples?
sven (Eng): Both would be helpful. Use `format=jsonl`, `page_size`, `page_token`. Note: in C# SDK method is `client.Audit.ExportAsync` returning IAsyncEnumerable<string>.
maya (DevEx): Draft C# snippet:
```csharp
var client = new RedwoodClient("TOKEN");
await foreach (var page in client.Audit.ExportAsync(new { since = "2026-01-01", format = "jsonl", page_size = 250 }))
{
    Console.WriteLine(page);
}
```
maya (DevEx): Draft PHP snippet (page-based):
```php
$client = new \Redwood\Client(getenv('TOKEN'));
$iterator = $client->audit->export(['since' => '2026-01-01', 'format' => 'jsonl', 'page_size' => 200]);
foreach ($iterator as $chunk) {
  echo $chunk;
}
```
kevin (Security): Add a short caveats bullet: backups & archival may retain data beyond active retention windows; explain how to request purge & legal hold interactions.
leo (Legal): Approved wording. Tiny nit: prefer 'retention policy' in one spot: "per the customer's retention policy".
nana (Docs): Switched that phrase. Also added redacted JSONL example to show schema: {"timestamp":"2026-02-10T09:00:00Z","action":"delete","user_id":"acct_42","redacted":true}
maya (DevEx): Pushed snippets into PR and left comments about SDK method names for v0.8 -> v0.9 migration. Also added example showing `redact=true` param and `next_page_token` handling.
sven (Eng): minor: in C# example use a typed options object rather than anonymous for clarity. Not required for merge.
nana (Docs): Thanks everyone — merging when CI is green. I'll follow up with a short changelog entry noting docs + snippet additions and where we mention backup & hold caveats.
